">&#x0003e;250 nmol/L</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mean</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">SD</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Current</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">240 (16.75%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">738 (51.5%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">455 (31.75%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0 (0%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">68.33</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">28.95</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Current plus 1,000 IU<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-ijerph-06-00151">a</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">8 (1%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">477 (33%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">948 (66%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0 (0%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">93.33</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">28.95</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Current plus 2,000 IU<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn2-ijerph-06-00151">b</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0 (0%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">100 (7%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1,332 (93%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn4-ijerph-06-00151">**</xref> (&#x0003c;1%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">118.33</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">28.95</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn1-ijerph-06-00151"><label>a</label><p>Current plus 1,000 IU is the case where every participant takes an additional 1,000 IU/d VTD</p></fn><fn id="tfn2-ijerph-06-00151"><label>b</label><p> Current plus 2,000 IU is the case where every participant takes an additional 2,000 IU/d VTD</p></fn><fn id="tfn3-ijerph-06-00151"><label>*</label><p>Projections based on available evidence that 40 IU/d of VTD supplementation will raise serum 25(OH)D by about 1 nmol/L [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b84-ijerph-06-00151">84</xref>&#x02013;<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b86-ijerph-06-00151">86</xref>].</p></fn><fn id="tfn4-ijerph-06-00151"><label>**</label><p>One individual&#x02019;s projected levels went above 250 nmol/L with supplementation. This individual had high sun exposure, regular tanning bed usage, and no supplementation.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>